The Pythagorean identity $\sin^2\theta + \cos^2\theta = 1$ is central to trigonometry. The softmax
function is

$$ \sigma(z)[3mi = \frac{e^{z_i}}{\sum[0m{j=1}^{K} e^{z_j}} $$

which is used in classification models.

